<article class="env-remark" id="00F3CD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00F3CD">Remark <span data-tag="00F3CD">6.3.6.5</span>.</a> It is possible to formulate a converse to Proposition <a href="/tag/181F32" data-tag="181F32">6.3.6.4</a>. Namely, one can characterize the class of algebraic morphisms as the smallest class of geometric morphisms which contains all étale morphisms and is stable under certain kinds of filtered limits. However, it is necessarily to allow limits which are parametrized not just by filtered $\infty $-categories, but filtered <em>stacks</em> over $\infty $-topoi. The precise statement requires ideas which lie outside the scope of this book. </p>
